      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The district’s economy thrives on agriculture, producing prized Nam Doc Mai mangoes, coconuts, orchids, and lotus flowers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bang_Bon_district",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Wat Bang Bon, a notable Buddhist temple, sits beside the Chao Phraya River, offering a peaceful riverside setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/thailand/bangkok_bang-bon",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "To reach Bang Bon by public transit, hop on the BTS to Bang Wa Station and then transfer to a taxi or bus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/thailand/bangkok_bang-bon",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bang Bon is mainly residential, yet recent years have seen steady development and better transport links to central Bangkok.",
